@startuml CorrectnessProof
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequence {
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    ParticipantBorderColor #1565C0
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #E8F5E9
    LifeLineBorderColor #2E7D32
    NoteBackgroundColor #FFF9C4
    NoteBorderColor #F9A825
}

title Correctness Proof — Induction on |S| (Visited Set)\n"When node u is dequeued from PQ, d[u] = δ(s, u)"

participant "Source s" as S
participant "Priority Queue\n(Min-Heap)" as PQ
participant "Visited Set S\n(finalised nodes)" as VS
participant "Current Node u" as U
participant "Neighbour v" as V

note over S, V
  **Invariant (I):** For every node x ∈ S,  d[x] = δ(s, x)
  **Claim:** The invariant holds after each Dequeue operation.
end note

S -> PQ : Enqueue(s, 0)\nd[s] ← 0

note over S, PQ
  **Base Case (|S| = 0 → 1):**
  s is dequeued first with d[s] = 0 = δ(s, s). ✓
  No negative weights ⇒ d[s] cannot be improved.
end note

PQ -> U  : Dequeue() → u  (min d[u] in PQ)
U  -> VS : visited.Add(u)

note over U, VS
  **Inductive Step:**
  Assume for all x ∈ S (|S|=k), d[x] = δ(s, x).
  Suppose for contradiction d[u] > δ(s, u).
end note

note over PQ, VS
  **Sub-lemma (triangle inequality):**
  ∀ edge (x→y):  δ(s, y) ≤ δ(s, x) + w(x, y)
  Proof: If a shorter path to y existed via x,
  relaxation would have already set d[y] ≤ d[x]+w(x,y).
end note

note over U, VS
  **Contradiction argument:**
  Let p* = shortest path s → u.
  Let (x, y) be the first edge on p* leaving S.
  • d[x] = δ(s, x)  (by inductive hypothesis, x ∈ S)
  • After relaxing (x,y): d[y] ≤ δ(s,x) + w(x,y) = δ(s,y) ≤ δ(s,u)
  • But u was dequeued before y  ⇒  d[u] ≤ d[y] ≤ δ(s,u)
  • Yet d[u] ≥ δ(s,u) (distances can only overestimate) ⇒ d[u] = δ(s,u) ✓
  Contradiction. Therefore d[u] = δ(s,u). □
end note

U  -> V  : Relax edge (u → v):\nnewDist = d[u] + w(u,v)
V  -> PQ : if newDist < d[v]:\n  d[v] ← newDist\n  Enqueue(v, newDist)

note over V, PQ
  **Relaxation Lemma:**
  After Relax(u,v):  d[v] ≤ d[u] + w(u,v)
  Combined with correctness of d[u], this preserves
  the invariant for all neighbours of u.
end note

PQ -> U  : ... repeat until u == target or PQ empty ...

note over S, V
  **Termination:**
  Each node enters S at most once (HashSet check).
  |S| grows by 1 per iteration ⇒ at most V iterations.
  ∴ Algorithm always terminates. □

  **Optimal Substructure:**
  If p* = s→...→u→...→t is shortest,
  then the sub-path s→...→u is shortest for u too.
  Proof: by cut-and-paste argument (standard). □
end note

@enduml
